<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><!--
    Amar Vault backup policy (Sprint 3B, Task 3) — API 30 and below.

    NOTHING is backed up. The vault is offline-first and privacy-first: the Room
    database (OCR text, metadata, chat history), embedding index files, id mappings,
    AI models, and preferences are device-local only and are excluded explicitly.
    allowBackup="false" in the manifest is the primary opt-out; these rules are
    defense in depth for transport paths that consult fullBackupContent anyway.

    Native indexes and models are rebuildable/re-downloadable caches; the Room
    database is the source of truth and is intentionally NOT cloud-backed-up because
    it contains user content (OCR text of screenshots, receipts, documents).

    Single source of truth for this policy: docs/BACKUP_AND_PRIVACY.md
    Keep these rules consistent with data_extraction_rules.xml (API 31+).
-->
<full-backup-content>
    <exclude domain="root" path="." />
    <exclude domain="file" path="." />
    <exclude domain="database" path="." />
    <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="." />
    <exclude domain="external" path="." />
</full-backup-content>
